  "description": "KOCFUG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H106 Eu6 N4 O52 Zn6. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn3 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu5 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu6 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Zn4 (Zn) has 5 O neighbors; Zn5 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors; Zn6 (Zn) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.401-3.881 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.10-118.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C102H106Eu6N4O52Zn6. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 18 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
